{"name": "hm4-a-crash-over-a-behind-file-the-user-then-edits-reverts-the-stores-edit", "description": "Honeymoon 4 counterexample 1 (holon-space/holon-work#175, bugfunnel 2026-10-12-restart-while-an-org-file-is-behind-reverts-the-stores-edit). The store's edit (`Buy milk` -> `Buy milk oat`) is committed but its write-back stalls under churn, so hm4.org keeps the pre-edit bytes; the app then DIES with that write-back owed (CrashRestart), and while it is down the user retitles another headline in that same file (`Call mom` -> `Call dad`). Expected: the boot merges BOTH \u2014 the store keeps `Buy milk oat` and picks up `Call dad`. MEASURED 2026-10-12 (red, this is the bug): the store's edit is REVERTED to `Buy milk` in every layer (block_raw, loro, matview, org) while the user's `Call dad` lands. Cause: on a cold boot `last_projection` is empty, so the diff base is seeded from the STORE (crates/holon-filesystem/src/file_sync_controller.rs:5776-5786); only `last_projection_hash` persists (:788/:1798), so the merge has no record of the bytes Holon last wrote and reads the store's own unwritten edit as an external removal.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Loro", "Org", "Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer", "ActionEngine"]}}, "transitions": [{"WriteOrgFile": {"filename": "hm4.org", "blocks": [{"id": "block:hm4r-a", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Buy milk", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4r-a"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}, {"id": "block:hm4r-b", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Call mom", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4r-b"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}], "keyword_set": null}}, {"ArmWriteChurn": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:hm4r-a"}}, {"TypeChars": {"text": " oat"}}, {"PressKey": {"chord": ["escape"]}}, {"CrashRestart": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0", "retitle_while_down": {"block": "block:hm4r-b", "disk_text": "Call mom", "text": "Call dad"}}}]}
{"name": "hm4-an-abandoned-id-stamp-leaves-an-id-less-file-whose-blocks-lose-identity", "description": "Honeymoon 4 counterexample 2 (holon-space/holon-work#175, bugfunnel 2026-10-12-an-abandoned-id-stamp-leaves-an-id-less-org-file-whose-blocks-lose-identity). An external editor replays hm4b.org without any `:ID:` drawer while a churning writer stalls the write-back; the ingest reconciles the id-less file onto the existing rows, then the churn ENDS (DisarmWriteChurn) with no crash and no reboot. Expected: the owed write-back lands and re-stamps `:ID: hm4c-a`/`hm4c-b` into the file. MEASURED 2026-10-12 (red): the write-back is never retried, so the file stays id-less forever; every parse of it mints a fresh `Uuid::new_v4` (crates/holon-org-format/src/parser.rs:1566-1573), so `inv-blocks-match-ref/org` reports the two rows REPLACED by two fresh ids (identity loss, not duplication), and `inv-org-render-fixed-point` stays divergent for 5s. The red carries two registered known-red signatures with it (the abandoned stalled write-back, and the stale `writeback-degraded` condition after the churn ends).", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Loro", "Org", "Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer", "ActionEngine"]}}, "transitions": [{"WriteOrgFile": {"filename": "hm4b.org", "blocks": [{"id": "block:hm4c-a", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Buy milk", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4c-a"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}, {"id": "block:hm4c-b", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Call mom", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4c-b"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}], "keyword_set": null}}, {"ArmWriteChurn": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"StaleExternalRewrite": {"doc_uri": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"DisarmWriteChurn": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}]}
{"name": "hm4-a-crash-over-a-file-only-behind-its-store-keeps-the-stores-edit", "description": "GREEN control for hm4-a-crash-over-a-behind-file-the-user-then-edits-reverts-the-stores-edit: the same crash with the file only BEHIND (nobody edits it while the app is down). MEASURED 2026-10-12: green \u2014 the boot finds the file byte-identical to the hash it recorded for the bytes it last wrote, so it takes no external edit and the store's `Buy milk oat` reaches disk. It isolates the user's edit while down as the load-bearing precondition of the revert.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Loro", "Org", "Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer", "ActionEngine"]}}, "transitions": [{"WriteOrgFile": {"filename": "hm4.org", "blocks": [{"id": "block:hm4r-a", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Buy milk", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4r-a"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}, {"id": "block:hm4r-b", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Call mom", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4r-b"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}], "keyword_set": null}}, {"ArmWriteChurn": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"FocusEditableText": {"block_id": "block:hm4r-a"}}, {"TypeChars": {"text": " oat"}}, {"PressKey": {"chord": ["escape"]}}, {"CrashRestart": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}]}
{"name": "hm4-a-crash-over-an-id-less-file-re-stamps-its-ids-at-boot", "description": "GREEN control for hm4-an-abandoned-id-stamp-leaves-an-id-less-file-whose-blocks-lose-identity: the id-less rewrite is followed by a CRASH (the churn ends with the process) rather than by the churn stopping under a live app. MEASURED 2026-10-12: green \u2014 the boot re-ingests the id-less file and re-stamps the ids, so identity survives. It isolates the live-app path (the write-back that is owed when the stall clears and never retried) as the defect.", "initial_state": {"wiring": {"storage_adapters": ["Loro", "Org", "Turso"], "sync_adapters": [], "actors": ["MCPServer", "ActionEngine"]}}, "transitions": [{"WriteOrgFile": {"filename": "hm4b.org", "blocks": [{"id": "block:hm4c-a", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Buy milk", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4c-a"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}, {"id": "block:hm4c-b", "parent_id": "block:gen-placeholder", "content": "Call mom", "content_type": "text", "source_language": null, "source_name": null, "properties": {"ID": "hm4c-b"}, "marks": null, "collapsed": false, "created_at": 0, "updated_at": 0}], "keyword_set": null}}, {"ArmWriteChurn": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"StaleExternalRewrite": {"doc_uri": "block:ref-doc-0"}}, {"CrashRestart": {"doc": "block:ref-doc-0"}}]}
